ncept", "title": "Hard edges"}, {"id": "59a6e395-76c5-48fd-9a12-1d79216f39de", "type": "concept", "title": "Soft edges"}, {"id": "fe75c839-b023-4b2c-ba6d-ae894220c346", "type": "concept", "title": "Occluding edges"}, {"id": "bbd66ce3-fe68-42d5-8880-078bbe855897", "type": "concept", "title": "Edge hierarchy"}], "description": "Gist: Edges help viewers understand form, depth, softness, focus, and material change."}, {"id": "d1484048-3225-44f5-ab36-e7d4a5441132", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accuracy checks", "children": [{"id": "56f6d945-0865-4ee2-8180-be17ef2e0588", "type": "concept", "title": "Plumb lines"}, {"id": "73c27906-a4a5-4101-aca7-b18b22df684b", "type": "concept", "title": "Angle sighting"}, {"id": "3452c49c-2712-4b56-8d48-67a0000b3f99", "type": "concept", "title": "Envelope method"}, {"id": "49a9ef4f-c830-45ab-8881-da5d7249f911", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative measurement"}], "description": "Gist: Designers need repeatable methods for finding and fixing proportion errors."}]}, {"id": "faa14580-b646-419e-8fe9-67d2349a989d", "type": "topic", "title": "Shape, Form, and Volume", "description": "Move from flat shapes to believable three-dimensional forms that can support products, spaces, figures, and visual systems.", "children": [{"id": "3d2d873f-9a89-4731-b279-a24f933d7d37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shape language", "children": [{"id": "6fcfe627-e57d-4320-acf3-5c5dcfd62b30", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometric shapes"}, {"id": "c18faa97-200b-4a50-9ea8-5f75bb211ffa", "type": "concept", "title": "Organic shapes"}, {"id": "c6f290c8-3d3e-4de4-b79f-705daa4dcabe", "type": "concept", "title": "Silhouette"}, {"id": "6526f512-9249-434b-bb3b-22385fe6b905", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative shape"}], "description": "Gist: Shape choices influence recognition, mood, balance, and design identity."}, {"id": "91671f88-6616-4739-8279-447a9b05b7de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Constructive form", "children": [{"id": "1f73ed00-12cb-4602-816e-4aa6eda63918", "type": "concept", "title": "Boxes"}, {"id": "a34365de-0aed-4e06-a5e4-6240d8381182", "type": "concept", "title": "Cylinders"}, {"id": "312be011-f6f9-4540-8324-79c871e5c864", "type": "concept", "title": "Spheres"}, {"id": "e61eb699-00bd-4587-b6b5-aaf9b53948ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Form combinations"}], "description": "Gist: Complex objects become manageable when built from simple forms."}, {"id": "1dbebd4c-0800-4c79-932b-870b5d6e4f93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Volume and overlap", "children": [{"id": "fcb0a713-63a5-487a-8926-05c3b64bab8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Overlapping forms"}, {"id": "bb182c7e-16af-4b63-936e-aefa316bd1c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Plane changes"}, {"id": "0524bec3-cfbc-4d7b-beec-0ced85e5c5c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreshortening"}, {"id": "7a8a24c8-7cb3-44fe-a588-8298d178312a", "type": "concept", "title": "Section thinking"}], "description": "Gist: Volume drawing helps students show how forms occupy and interact in space."}]}, {"id": "bfb1c6d8-cfea-4284-9566-70322a42b7bc", "type": "topic", "title": "Value, Light, and Tonal Structure", "description": "Use light, shadow, and value organization to clarify form, hierarchy, mood, and spatial depth.", "children": [{"id": "b86d4b10-de26-45bc-90d8-1a0d134099af", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Value scales", "children": [{"id": "fd43adb0-1beb-486f-902d-81306febd0ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Five-step scales"}, {"id": "f30908de-7c55-43e7-b305-fd973769e262", "type": "concept", "title": "Full tonal range"}, {"id": "01132b2d-d71a-49d3-bb18-03329eb33399", "type": "concept", "title": "Local value"}, {"id": "2a33abe1-740c-4a87-9860-a7e3a7e28b17", "type": "concept", "title": "Value grouping"}], "description": "Gist: A controlled value range lets students organize drawings with clarity and depth."}, {"id": "bee09dfd-9044-4cf8-ab45-afdd95530553", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Light logic", "children": [{"id": "2fe70c89-f2d2-4558-a971-38eb164d8281", "type": "concept", "title": "Light source"}, {"id": "d81bc82c-9696-4459-8ff6-aa35551f4884", "type": "concept", "title": "Core shadow"}, {"id": "e4bf0fa3-b72f-44ad-bcc4-07e231c1210e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cast shadow"}, {"id": "62b7e85f-b9a5-495e-9421-f93e3a473476", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflected light"}], "description": "Gist: Understanding light turns shading into a reasoned system rather than decoration."}, {"id": "425e741b-56ea-4c28-a61a-0d2a04c8ebab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tonal composition", "children": [{"id": "221f4eb2-b2ec-4c3d-aa68-d3d1e87e97f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Focal contrast"}, {"id": "81734bc7-e8ba-4c41-ab1e-a9c6980b6d05", "type": "concept", "title": "Massed shadows"}, {"id": "7cc7db0b-b8fb-4467-9199-985a81fa9d5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Atmospheric depth"}, {"id": "06c87f2d-630b-4384-8bca-a40eb1198582", "type": "concept", "title": "Notan studies"}], "description": "Gist: Value structure guides attention and makes drawings readable from a distance."}]}, {"id": "c53e0660-6090-4383-be4d-3a5d2e90dcb2", "type": "topic", "title": "Perspective and Spatial Construction", "description": "Construct convincing space through horizon lines, vanishing points, ellipses, scale, and viewpoint control.", "children": [{"id": "8a64889e-2c92-44fd-800a-22a12c3e437c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Linear perspective", "children": [{"id": "1016135f-dfd3-4a45-9539-806c3191fdae", "type": "concept", "title": "Horizon line"}, {"id": "200a4f81-a02c-4252-921a-225abc1fbf20", "type": "concept", "title": "One-point perspective"}, {"id": "d6255291-a68b-4f7f-98e1-067d053246a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Two-point perspective"}, {"id": "fd698451-153c-4755-87d3-b576c43a92b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Three-point perspective"}], "description": "Gist: Perspective gives designers a reliable way to invent and evaluate believable space."}, {"id": "e440000a-c9fc-4ae0-aa6f-bb3b1aa99ec3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ellipses and cylinders", "children": [{"i