pic", "title": "Scale relationships", "children": [{"id": "a67dde40-8c1a-4b2a-96eb-53fa0f344a21", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-to-large studies"}, {"id": "09f832e4-caf3-48bf-b7c3-0314f41b0b87", "type": "concept", "title": "Focal scale"}, {"id": "07a067d0-9187-4f6b-afd8-9d2fd9bafb56", "type": "concept", "title": "Human scale"}, {"id": "80fb8e29-8dda-4895-b758-5dc84d35b667", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative scale"}], "description": "Gist: Scale helps drawings communicate importance, distance, function, and hierarchy."}, {"id": "166232cc-1ffb-41d8-883c-7d8d7a28d341", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sequencing", "children": [{"id": "f3efd012-3543-40d4-9090-1452b59f07e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Process panels"}, {"id": "03fb4c66-c196-4c48-aa0d-1f974b30ac45", "type": "concept", "title": "Storyboard logic"}, {"id": "7f9217f2-7374-4dab-bea8-0298a6292aab", "type": "concept", "title": "Before-after studies"}, {"id": "b6e658eb-e87f-41fd-b560-323eeaa3aa19", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation flow"}], "description": "Gist: Designers often need several drawings to tell one idea clearly."}]}, {"id": "06319866-1497-433f-9e07-c235f227ddc3", "type": "topic", "title": "Proportion, Measurement, and Figure/Object Relationships", "description": "Develop measuring strategies for objects, bodies, environments, and the relationships among them.", "children": [{"id": "7afbbdbc-46bf-4601-8293-2e4ea1ce4411", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative proportion", "children": [{"id": "22d89f62-b228-4e34-80e1-0f9ce70816b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit measurement"}, {"id": "04f7e1cb-245a-4863-8b48-da4fc3a5356f", "type": "concept", "title": "Angle comparison"}, {"id": "9254e574-4ce2-4805-966a-50e7b35a91d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative height and width"}, {"id": "50da37ea-ff76-49f9-9c2a-dc2da1b1efa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Landmarks"}], "description": "Gist: Proportion skills help students draw objects and figures as organized relationships rather than isolated parts."}, {"id": "ee312f66-ed41-4c6b-a5cd-edfefca9fa33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Figure basics for designers", "children": [{"id": "a096c3a3-fac8-4a9b-984f-c459ac39cd5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture and balance"}, {"id": "9fcf33b6-1e7f-4b44-8ea5-42409078e3a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Simple anatomy landmarks"}, {"id": "bfc22027-bf92-4905-856d-e00115b618cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Hands and faces overview"}, {"id": "8a444a2f-7cf9-4db4-be83-2d9bc02e8ae2", "type": "concept", "title": "Clothed figure studies"}], "description": "Gist: Even non-illustrators need enough figure knowledge to show bodies, users, scale, and interaction."}, {"id": "488ce3e9-123a-4739-b019-d00ba851be49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Objects in context", "children": [{"id": "5a0e517e-0aab-4e4f-8223-cb27dd3f9744", "type": "concept", "title": "Object groups"}, {"id": "824bf165-2b90-42fd-b62f-00c7effee852", "type": "concept", "title": "Contact shadows"}, {"id": "038b431f-197d-44f4-98e5-47ab6fe3d570", "type": "concept", "title": "User interaction"}, {"id": "6d4330db-9451-449f-8838-df3f6aeb6b45", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental scale"}], "description": "Gist: Design drawing becomes stronger when objects relate to users, surfaces, spaces, and systems."}]}, {"id": "c90b0d85-cb26-4349-9603-1231f2c0bfcc", "type": "topic", "title": "Texture, Surface, and Material Description", "description": "Describe material behavior through mark, value, edge, density, pattern, and surface logic.", "children": [{"id": "72b86f7e-136a-4484-9326-c3a31fd1ccd4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texture vocabulary", "children": [{"id": "90d9547a-725a-4b87-bfda-e61de8828137", "type": "concept", "title": "Rough and smooth"}, {"id": "3994a776-4cf4-4aa2-a3bd-2f89488ef6c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Gloss and matte"}, {"id": "584b0b11-ac96-48de-b040-804286cfaa84", "type": "concept", "title": "Grain"}, {"id": "b0ed47a6-7ede-47ee-ae7f-da8484e68ded", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeated irregularity"}], "description": "Gist: Texture drawings teach students to distinguish surface facts from decorative patterns."}, {"id": "ad57f252-7b20-406e-adfb-875b6e705462", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material rendering", "children": [{"id": "0f3bc31e-04c7-4b77-a6bd-b9334a5a35a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Metal"}, {"id": "9c56feee-9ada-4482-afef-931ec845b2c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Glass"}, {"id": "e3b7ca97-ebf1-4c60-b8c8-c35e67a31801", "type": "concept", "title": "Fabric"}, {"id": "8075a5be-fbad-49f7-b669-2ae31e930b62", "type": "concept", "title": "Wood and paper"}], "description": "Gist: Material description helps viewers infer what something is made of and how it behaves."}, {"id": "b1801cfa-9a3f-4605-8a00-433aba6ec3ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surface as meaning", "children": [{"id": "263ff814-84e0-487e-986c-e80cecd08451", "type": "concept", "title": "Wear and patina"}, {"id": "4e239ad1-fa9c-4fd2-ab40-9a243e3776fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleanliness and finish"}, {"id": "8f1a440d-f605-430f-9e27-c91e111662d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern systems"}, {"id": "6efb9c38-2736-4b56-acda-b332375e8174", "type": "concept", "title": "Material contrast"}], "description": "Gist: Surfaces can carry mood, use, age, brand, and cultural meaning."}]}, {"id": "36f01be2-411e-4dd5-ba3d-b8e18b40a121", "type": "topic", "title": "Diagramming, Ideation, and Visual Notes", "description": "Use fast drawing systems to capture research, map relationships, generate alternatives, and explain decisions.", "children": [{"id": "46321c9f-bc69-41e0-a3dc-5f63f1345fa4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual note-taking", "children": [{"id": "36863af4-cb85-4faa-8204-bb5fd637dc60", "type": "concept", "title": "Hierarchy of notes"}, {"id": "36a0e726-5d59-4eb1-a61f-288b72485075", "type": "concept", "title": "Icons and symbols"}, {"id": "5b8267f9-2b94-4e76-82d6-ce7f0ee158ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Callouts"}, {"id": "fe356b07-a967-4ab7-95d1-9d46a58b1588", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept mapping"}], "description": "Gist: Visual notes help students capture lectures, research, interviews, and observations in usable form."}, {"id": "631359d5-e7e1-4f99-8f0c-09c91f8ae553", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ideation sketching", "children": [{"id": "d77af022-bde7-4d8d-9a05-04575f2cd870", "type": "concept", "title": "Fluency"}, {"id": "b6a4da28-e62a-49b2-8367-1e8e3b82e93d", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation"}, {"id": "bc6ef386-b950-4b59-b290-cdd70e1d1c57", "type": "concept", "title": "Combination"}, {"id": "871fcead-2178-4fd9-9b06-8f838881b2b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection criteria"}], "description": "Gist: Rapid sketching generates multiple options before students over-invest in one solution."}, {"id": "1e69ead6-1cdf-4a0f-afbb-029ea7ccaced", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagrams and systems", "children": [{"id": "741b2026-8a6f-4488-ab17-7ead3ec7f330", "type": "concept", "title": "Flow diagrams"}, {"id": "08e93f31-715b-460c-9a11-d562de9472e5", "type": "concept", "title": "User journeys"}, {"id": "6f1a6a6c-40a9-4ea0-96b8-ac9050db62d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploded diagrams"}, {"id": "b5926e2b-2af8-46f5-ab5e-d517f6aa3b48", "type": "concept", "title": "Cause-effect maps"}], "description": "Gist: Diagrams make invisible relationships, sequences, and causes visible."}]}, {"id": "8e06b337-654b-4fac-b663-4bd8c92f7789", "type": "topic", "title": "Color, Mixed Media, and Presentation Studies", "description": "Introduce color and mixed media as tools for visual emphasis, atmosphere, material exploration, and presentation readiness.", "children": [{"id": "37d92b4c-ea0a-45b3-a93a-495985a7c406", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color as structure", "children": [{"id": "771120b8-6e17-4dd8-ae94-9a36131c1436", "type": "concept", "title": "Hue"}, {"id": "2c0d09b6-89ec-4f18-9df1-7ef2a164ca7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Value and saturation"}, {"id": "7b14ce94-16db-41b1-bf4c-8d44340b9b02", "type": "concept", "title": "Limited palettes"}, {"id": "4e0a44cc-0513-4ecc-8f62-684785bbe838", "type": "concept", "title": "Color hierarchy"}], "description": "Gist: Color can organize attention, separate information layers, and support emotional tone."}, {"id": "63f05f26-2795-4cb5-8a71-dca1f1762cb5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-media exploration", "children": [{"id": "9c208a8e-64a2-4833-be09-18b6f625dddd", "type": "concept", "title": "Ink and wash"}, {"id": "3d714697-73f9-4870-b06c-beaf93125bcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Collage"}, {"id": "4990729e-14ea-4d1d-b836-03f6b00da6c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Marker and pencil"}, {"id": "ae1351c8-f197-4b76-97cb-52fdf6370a6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Opaque and transparent layers"}], "description": "Gist: Combining media helps students discover new marks, textures, and presentation effects."}, {"id": "c379b53f-7419-4058-b854-688009ed6611", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation studies", "children": [{"id": "d04baec4-2413-481d-b1ed-57446c3bcfcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Mounting"}, {"id": "1da6c32a-a381-4194-934b-512030a2fccc", "type": "concept", "title": "Labels"}, {"id": "d92bec6a-3f57-4d1e-8d64-93f924f52ce2", "type": "concept", "title": "Series consistency"}, {"id": "13d8e22a-935d-44a5-820b-cfdc5eee58e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Craft standards"}], "description": "Gist: A drawing study becomes more useful when it is clean, legible, and ready for critique."}]}, {"id": "2454dcb5-8e6d-4f21-8b2b-ea290db5b55a", "type": "topic", "title": "Drawing for Typography, Layout, and Graphic Systems", "description": "Connect drawing practice to graphic design through lettering, hierarchy, grids, icons, and visual systems.", "children": [{"id": "35a8cd88-c2ef-427a-98d3-491aea9d4071", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hand lettering and type studies", "children": [{"id": "c80e372d-31d4-4351-bb77-1d57a503e197", "type": "concept", "title": "Letter anatomy"}, {"id": "8281eb85-96d3-42bc-9de6-e8ee84262310", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline and x-height"}, {"id": "50b423f2-3156-4244-bcb3-8bf25da6072f", "type": "concept", "title": "Kerning"}, {"id": "23ee71b1-b910-4d74-a892-6106b79d1638", "type": "concept", "title": "Expressive lettering"}], "description": "Gist: Drawing type trains attention to proportion, spacing, rhythm, and the personality of letterforms."}, {"id": "3129365e-2288-4567-a47e-8d7da97d38e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layout sketching", "children": [{"id": "1e3c66df-d39c-4f0e-86cd-8163935c4fa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Grid thumbnails"}, {"id": "04378fa6-22a1-49b2-a806-46968fa66a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Image-text relationships"}, {"id": "1af728db-89d3-44aa-9238-9ed96a4e57b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Modular layouts"}, {"id": "f5f64b42-8bdd-4e03-9bca-b42065b730a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Composition alternatives"}], "description": "Gist: Quick layout drawings let designers test hierarchy before moving into software."}, {"id": "5bd55285-0547-4ef5-9d7c-728f94b7de2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Icons and visual systems", "children": [{"id": "6726a76d-4883-4fe9-838b-fa7c0dc82348", "type": "concept", "title": "Pictograms"}, {"id": "f5a981d1-48b2-4073-b467-981bab6a8bda", "type": "concept", "title": "Simplification"}, {"id": "8535b569-8763-40cf-87d0-fbf507d91551", "type": "concept", "title": "Style rules"}, {"id": "e308707a-80ea-449c-9c30-46032b262cb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Symbol families"}], "description": "Gist: Icon drawing teaches reduction, consistency, metaphor, and system thinking."}]}, {"id": "9f3c68f3-f8aa-40f4-acdd-31cb3230b55d", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Drawing, Tablets, and Hybrid Workflows", "description": "Blend hand drawing with digital tools for iteration, cleanup, layering, annotation, and portfolio production.", "children": [{"id": "7a7065a0-4b36-4de5-899f-19c643564e72", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital drawing basics", "children": [{"id": "a5d0482b-5362-41e2-8959-9aa8dc6d87d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Tablet setup"}, {"id": "d43982f6-1280-4392-8b88-8a73d0d43034", "type": "concept", "title": "Brush control"}, {"id": "0a8f3304-5dc6-4ae8-906d-353508035849", "type": "concept", "title": "Layer discipline"}, {"id": "668f02fc-8e6e-417a-ae58-6f0952e9a31e", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming"}], "description": "Gist: Digital tools extend drawing through layers, undo, opacity, brushes, and rapid duplication."}, {"id": "c6a18635-c961-4457-8fed-aaa569de3e30", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybrid cleanup and iteration", "children": [{"id": "2cdf2765-7754-481b-bcf9-3f14114527af", "type": "concept", "title": "Scanning"}, {"id": "2e2bd99c-4d2f-475a-b6d7-d258f13de8be", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast cleanup"}, {"id": "0792bb9c-6ca0-42b1-8515-c49b35bf447b", "type": "concept", "title": "Overlay drawing"}, {"id": "c2d24f52-3d92-4fa5-8a15-0e7fdbe79451", "type": "concept", "title": "Versioning"}], "description": "Gist: Hand sketches can be scanned, corrected, annotated, colored, and developed digitally."}, {"id": "8e99599c-b110-40c2-918a-fa9776d44a88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible digital workflow", "children": [{"id": "120187e6-1af0-4dde-bf44-f0495469bf7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference ethics"}, {"id": "dc4be9e2-f456-414b-9d5c-994ef1457d48", "type": "concept", "title": "AI and authorship discussion"}, {"id": "7a774307-1b62-4174-9b7f-fa17f9e91907", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility of files"}, {"id": "25099280-f3a7-43ee-ba9f-15cb4ba84bab", "type": "concept", "title": "Export formats"}], "description": "Gist: Digital speed should support thinking, not replace observation or craft."}]}, {"id": "7c7e38ad-a95a-498a-bf51-9d06117abf31", "type": "topic", "title": "Visual Research, Precedent, and Iteration", "description": "Develop research-led drawing processes informed by precedent, audience, context, and repeated revision.", "children": [{"id": "3f35f4c5-8e69-44b0-bfdc-d59b0708b4ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Precedent study", "children": [{"id": "c7cf